      "id": 1,
      "text": "Carbon Hill was settled in 1886 because of coal mining and the railroad.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbon_Hill%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town grew around the Galloway Coal Company, which bought mines in 1890 for $130,000.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbon_Hill%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Carbon Hill incorporated on February 14, 1891, the same day as Valentine’s Day, earning the nickname “Village of Love and Luck.”.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbon_Hill%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A post office opened in 1887 with John T. Anderson as its first postmaster.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbon_Hill%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The first United Methodist Church in Carbon Hill was built by 1888, reflecting early community growth.",
